---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import CareerBreakCalculator from '../../components/tools/CareerBreakCalculator.astro';
const schema={'@context':'https://schema.org','@type':'WebApplication',name:'Career Break and Maternity Leave Impact Calculator',url:'https://dollarangle.com/tools/career-break-maternity-leave-calculator',operatingSystem:'Any',applicationCategory:'FinanceApplication',isAccessibleForFree:true,description:'Estimate the immediate cash and potential retirement savings impact of parental leave or time away from work.'};
const faqs=[['What does the calculator include?','It estimates after-deduction earnings forgone, income from paid leave, avoided childcare and work expenses, missed employer and employee retirement contributions, and their hypothetical future value.'],['Can dads or other caregivers use it?','Yes. This is for maternity leave, paternity leave, adoption leave or any temporary career break.'],['Does it calculate government leave benefits?','No. Enter the relevant paid leave as a percentage of your normal gross salary. Check your actual entitlement and tax treatment locally.'],['Is projected retirement loss guaranteed?','No. Investment growth is hypothetical, and retirement plans differ. The future-value scenario assumes missed monthly contributions and a constant illustrative annual return.']];
---
<BaseLayout title="Career Break & Maternity Leave Calculator | DollarAngle" description="Free maternity leave and career break calculator. Estimate lost take-home pay, paid parental leave, avoided childcare costs and potential retirement impact.">
<script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(schema)}/>
<div class="container page"><nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a> › <a href="/tools">Money Tools</a> › Career Break Calculator</nav>
<header class="intro"><p class="kicker">FREE CAREER & FAMILY FINANCE CALCULATOR</p><h1>Career Break & Maternity Leave: <span>Calculate the Financial Impact</span></h1><p>Taking parental leave or stepping away from work may affect both your current budget and long-term savings. Explore a customizable scenario without reducing the decision to a single number.</p></header>
<CareerBreakCalculator/>
<article class="guide"><h2>How does maternity leave affect finances?</h2><p>Income may drop during unpaid leave or while receiving a reduced paid-leave benefit. But some costs can also fall, such as commuting and childcare. The calculator subtracts paid leave and avoided costs from estimated full-pay take-home income to model an immediate cash difference.</p>
<h2>Long-term retirement and savings effects</h2><p>Taking time out can interrupt employee and employer retirement contributions. The model estimates contributions not made during the break and grows those missing amounts at your chosen illustrative rate. It is not an individualized pension projection and does not account for promotions, changing earnings, vesting, market volatility or benefits specific to your plan.</p>
<h2>Make the comparison useful for your family</h2><p>Enter your actual salary, effective deduction assumptions, paid-leave policy, childcare expenses and retirement contributions. Compare different break lengths or paid-leave percentages. Check government benefits, job protection and pension eligibility separately for your location.</p>
<h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>{faqs.map(([q,a])=><details><summary>{q}</summary><p>{a}</p></details>)}
<h2>Related Money Tools</h2><p><a href="/tools/stay-at-home-parent-calculator">Should One Parent Stay Home? →</a> <a href="/tools/mine-yours-ours-budget-calculator">Build a Couples Budget →</a></p>
<p class="note">Illustrative financial planning only, not tax, investment, workplace, pension or legal advice. Currency selection changes the label only. Verify leave payments and pension rules with your employer or relevant authority.</p></article></div></BaseLayout>
